            },
            {
              "line_number": 1080,
              "content": "  <p>Engineering phases (Phase 0…6 in <a href=\"#roadmap\">Implementation Roadmap</a>) are execution slices. <strong>Product milestones</strong> below are what contributors and users orient on. See <a href=\"#adr-0020\">ADR-0020</a>.</p>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 1181,
              "content": "            <td><a href=\"#adr-0020\">ADR-0020</a></td>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 1197,
              "content": "            <td><a href=\"#adr-0004\">ADR-0004</a>, <a href=\"#adr-0017\">ADR-0017</a></td>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 1213,
              "content": "            <td><a href=\"#adr-0002\">ADR-0002</a>, <a href=\"#adr-0018\">ADR-0018</a></td>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 1221,
              "content": "            <td><a href=\"#adr-0020\">ADR-0020</a></td>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 1229,
              "content": "            <td><a href=\"#adr-0011\">ADR-0011</a></td>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 1242,
              "content": "  <p>Large monorepos fail when “everything depends on everything.” NVide uses four visibility tiers. Enforced by crate features, <code>pub(crate)</code> discipline, and CI dependency allowlists. See <a href=\"#adr-0012\">ADR-0012</a>.</p>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 1317,
              "content": "  <p>Multiple version clocks exist on purpose. Do not conflate product release with plugin ABI. See <a href=\"#adr-0016\">ADR-0016</a>, <a href=\"#adr-0011\">ADR-0011</a>.</p>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 1524,
              "content": "  <p>Rust correctness at IDE scale depends on explicit ownership. Default: <strong>one owner, many borrowed readers, Arc only at process/service boundaries</strong>. See <a href=\"#adr-0013\">ADR-0013</a>.</p>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 1612,
              "content": "  <p>Unify failure handling early so contributors do not invent per-crate conventions. See <a href=\"#adr-0014\">ADR-0014</a>.</p>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 1948,
              "content": "    <p>See also <a href=\"#crate-ownership\">Crate Ownership</a>, <a href=\"#dependency-diagram\">Dependency Diagram</a>, and <a href=\"#adr-0012\">ADR-0012</a>.</p>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 2130,
              "content": "          <tr><td>Terminal panel</td><td>Multiplexed terminals</td><td><a href=\"#terminal\">Terminal</a> · <a href=\"#adr-0015\">ADR-0015</a></td></tr>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 3025,
              "content": "  <p>Testing is a product requirement, not an afterthought. Gates are defined in <a href=\"#adr-0019\">ADR-0019</a>. No merge to <code>main</code> with red required checks.</p>"
            },
            {
              "line_number": 3348,
              "content": "    <p>The canonical ADR catalog is at the <strong>front</strong> of this document: <a href=\"#adr-catalog\">Architecture Decision Record Catalog</a> (<a href=\"#adr-0001\">ADR-0001</a> … <a href=\"#adr-0020\">ADR-0020</a>+). This section exists so older links to <code>#adr-index</code> still resolve.</p>"
            }
